Because we can.

Seriously, spaces are often* unneeded, and running cmavo together into=20
"cmavo clusters" can be clearer. A good example is with numbers, where I'd=
=20
prefer to say {li pano} =3D "the-number 10", rather than {li pa no} (which =
is=20
like writing "the-number 1 0"). Cmavo clusters are easy to split up; each=
=20
cmavo starts with a consonant (other than apostrophe, but including full=20
stop), which is followed by vowels, and maybe an apostrophe.

*(Not important:) If stress is marked (as it is in speech), no spaces are=
=20
needed. Stress/spaces are needed to distinguish between {rodbo'e bai ko'a}=
=20
and {rodbo'ebai ko'a}. Written with no spaces, they are {rodb=F3'ebaik=F3'a=
}=20
and {rodbo'=E9baik=F3'a}, respectively.

